      "target": "../sections/sec-001-process-for-managing-declarations-and-conflicts.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "In September 2010, the External Review Group (ERG) met to decide on the update of Comprehensive \ncervical cancer control: a guide to essential practice (C4-GEP), which was originally published \nin 2006. One of the major conclusions was that the chapter on screening and treatment of \nprecancerous lesions for cervical cancer prevention needed to be updated. This group also made \nrecommendations to the World Health Organization (WHO) on the composition of the Guideline \nDevelopment Group (GDG).\nIn 2011, the GDG and the Methods Group (MG) met several times in joint sessions to develop the \nPICO qu",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Recounts how the guideline arose from a 2010 decision to update WHO's 2006 guide to comprehensive cervical cancer control, and how the guideline groups developed PICO questions, outcomes and a modelling approach in 2011–2012. It notes that the guideline covers screening and treatment of precancerous lesions, not HPV vaccination, although the section title refers to managing conflicts of interest.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
